details:
(a) whether Government has operationalised the Next Generation DNA Sequencing Facility and Digital Wildlife Information Systems for strengthening wildlife conservation and research;
(b) the objectives, expenditure incurred and major features of these facilities;
(c) whether these facilities would be used for genetic profiling, wildlife forensics, disease surveillance and monitoring of endangered species;
(d) whether the State Forest Departments and protected areas are proposed to be integrated with the digital platform; and
(e) the steps taken to promote technology-driven wildlife conservation, real-time data sharing and capacity building across the country?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review of digitization and digital archival management initiatives of the National Archives of India through the 'Abhilekh Patal' platform;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of progress made under the platform with regard to digitization, metadata standardization and expansion of digital archival repository; 
(d) whether measures have been taken to strengthen digital accessibility, archival search capabilities and integration of emerging technologies to improve public access to archival records; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of achievements of Sanchar Saathi portal and mobile application in preventing telecom-related fraud since its launch;
(b) whether any institutional mechanism exists for coordination between DoT, banks and law enforcement agencies through the Digital Intelligence Platform to act on fraud reports in real time;
(c) the steps being taken to ensure accessibility of Sanchar Saathi services across regional languages and among first-time mobile users;
(d) if so, whether any measures have been taken to mandate availability of Sanchar Saathi app on mobile devices sold in India; and
(e) the future roadmap for strengthening citizen-centric telecom security tools under Sanchar Saathi?

(a) the progress made in the development of Wayside Amenities (WSAs) along National Highways, including facilities such as rest areas, food courts, fuel stations, emergency medical services and public conveniences;
(b) the status of development of Electric Vehicle (EV) charging infrastructure along major National Highway corridors, including the number of operational and proposed charging stations;
(c) whether Government is promoting Public-Private Partnership for development of Wayside Amenities and EV charging infrastructure and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected impact of these initiatives on road safety, tourism, employment generation, logistics efficiency and regional economic development?

(a) the salient features of the National Investment Policy for Urea-2026 (NIPU-2026) approved by Government and the objectives sought to be achieved thereunder;
(b) the measures proposed under the Policy to promote new investments in gas-based urea manufacturing units and enhance domestic urea production;
(c) the manner in which the Policy is expected to improve transparency, provide a viable return on investment and reduce foreign exchange risks for investors; and
(d) the expected impact of NIPU-2026 on achieving self-reliance in urea production, reducing imports and ensuring long-term fertilizer security for farmers?

(a) the key features and implementation strategy of the modified UDAN scheme approved by Government;
(b) the targets under the modified UDAN scheme for development of new airports, aerodromes, helipads and regional air routes across the country;
(c) the measures taken to improve the financial viability and long-term sustainability of regional air connectivity, particularly in underserved, remote and aspirational areas; and
(d) the expected impact of the scheme on regional connectivity, tourism, employment generation, investment and balanced regional development under the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047?

(a) whether Government proposes to expand SARAS Aajeevika Galleries, SARAS Melas and eSARAS across the country, particularly in Rajasthan;
(b) whether any cities in Rajasthan have been identified for establishing SARAS Aajeevika Galleries or organizing regular SARAS Melas, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the measures proposed to ensure participation of women Self Help Groups (SHGs) from small towns, rural and aspirational districts of Rajasthan in these initiatives; and
(d) whether Government proposes to provide branding, packaging, digital marketing and export support to such SHGs, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key outcomes of the South Asian Policy Leadership for Improved Nutrition and Growth (SAPLING) Dialogue–2026 and the measures proposed to strengthen India's food processing ecosystem;
(b) the steps taken to promote value addition, reduce post-harvest losses and strengthen agricultural supply chains through food processing;
(c) the initiatives undertaken to promote investment, technology adoption and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) participation in the food processing sector; and
(d) the measures taken to enhance food processing levels, generate employment and improve farmers' income through the sector?

(a) the progress made by India Post Payments Bank in expanding financial inclusion through its newly launched SHG Savings Account for women-led Self Help Groups;
(b) whether Government has identified States and Union Territories for large-scale rollout of the scheme and the number of SHGs likely to benefit therefrom;
(c) the manner in which the extensive postal network is being utilised to provide accessible, paperless and doorstep banking services to SHGs; and
(d) the expected contribution of this initiative towards women empowerment, Digital India, rural entrepreneurship and inclusive economic growth?

(a) the progress made under Mission Shakti, Saksham Anganwadi & POSHAN 2.0, and Mission Vatsalya for women's empowerment, child nutrition and child protection;
(b) State-wise details, particularly in Rajasthan, of Anganwadi infrastructure upgraded, implementation of the POSHAN Tracker, adoption of technology-based monitoring and the progress made in reducing malnutrition; and
(c) State-wise details of children provided Sponsorship Assistance and rehabilitated through Child Care Institutions (CCIs) under Mission Vatsalya?

(a) whether Government is extending guidance and support to States for promoting mother tongue-based education in accordance with the National Education Policy (NEP), 2020, Article 350A of the Constitution and the Right to Education Act, 2009;
(b) the initiatives taken to promote Indian and regional languages through curriculum development, textbooks, teacher training and digital learning resources; and
(c) whether Government has taken note of recent judicial observations relating to the promotion of regional languages, including Rajasthani and the steps taken in this regard?

(a) the major achievements of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) during the last five years, including the number of cases resolved, recoveries achieved and companies revived;
(b) the measures taken to strengthen the insolvency ecosystem and improve resolution timelines and recovery rates;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any review of the implementation of the Code and if so, the key findings thereof; and
(d) the steps proposed to further strengthen the IBC framework in line with the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047?

(a) the present status of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM), including the number of rural households provided with tap water connections, particularly in the State of Rajasthan;
(b) the steps taken to provide tap water to the remaining villages, especially in desert and water-scarce areas of the State of Rajasthan;
(c) whether Government is using modern technology to monitor water supply and water quality under the Mission; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure regular, safe and sustainable drinking water supply in rural areas through community participation and proper maintenance of water supply systems?

(a) the progress made towards achieving the target of gasifying 100 million tonnes of coal by 2030, including the status of coal gasification projects under implementation;
(b) the policy, financial and coal linkage support provided by Government to promote coal gasification and underground coal gasification projects;
(c) the initiatives taken to promote collaboration with BRICS countries in clean coal technologies; and
(d) the expected impact of these initiatives on energy security, import substitution and value-added industrial production?

(a) the progress made under the LiFE (Lifestyle for Environment) Movement, so far;
(b) the key achievements in India’s climate action including Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs), renewable energy expansion and reduction of emission intensity;
(c) how these initiatives contribute towards India’s goal of becoming a developed nation with net-zero emissions by 2070; and
(d) the details of initiatives undertaken under the LiFE Movement, including in the State of Maharashtra?

(a) the objectives, components and present status of implementation of the Kala Sanskriti Vikas Yojana (KSVY);
(b) the details of financial assistance and cultural grants released under the scheme during the last three years, State-wise, including Rajasthan;
(c) the measures taken to promote traditional arts, folk culture, artists and cultural institutions through the scheme; and
(d) whether Government proposes to strengthen KSVY by expanding financial assistance, digital outreach and capacity-building programmes for artists and cultural organizations and if so, the details thereof?
